  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Every occupied bench needs the same short cleanup before its session ends, and cleaning supplies are available nearby.\", \"decision\": \"How should bench cleanup be organized?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers clean their own benches during the final minutes of their sessions using the posted checklist. Responsibility stays with the person who knows what was used, and the next member receives a ready surface.\nThe steward announces a cleanup pause before each bench session ends, and members clean their own surfaces together. A common reminder protects cleanup time when members are absorbed in finishing their projects.\nMembers working nearby pair up to clean one bench and then the other during their final session minutes. Shared effort makes overlooked scraps and tools easier to notice while both benches receive the same checklist."
    }
  ],
